  "narrative": "The newly delivered interaction panel (H165-H172) tests whether previously observed or untested contrasts are localized within median-split strata of continuous modifiers. This was the natural follow-up to the failure of marginal main-effect screens and the many validation reversals, but none of these eight interaction claims meets the evidential bar. H165 and H169-H172 have intervals that cross zero and point estimates that either oppose the registered direction or fall below the approximate 10% clinical-scale threshold. H167 and H172 are directionally positive for the registered negative-interaction hypothesis but are imprecise and clinically subthreshold. H166 (outcome_014 feature_063 interaction at high feature_039) and H168 (outcome_013 feature_064 interaction at high feature_051) have point estimates larger than the relevant 10% absolute-mean scale, which makes them superficially interesting, but both intervals include zero. Given eight new post-hoc interaction tests, unadjusted discovery intervals, prior instability of nominally significant findings, no remaining voluntary validation budget, and the possibility of residual confounding and correlated outcomes, these near-zero bounds do not justify acceptance. The best-supported interpretation is that this dataset does not currently show scientifically meaningful effect modification for the tested interactions. I therefore reject and close all eight due claims. The accepted set remains empty.",
